      "text": "To find the product of \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and determine the coefficients \\(a, b, c, d\\), we start by expanding the expression using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\nFirst, let's distribute each term in \\(3x^2 - 5x + 4\\) to each term in \\(7 - 2x\\):\n\n1. Distribute \\(3x^2\\):\n\\[3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2\\]\n\\[3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3\\]\n2. Distribute \\(-5x\\):\n\\[-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x\\]\n\\[-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2\\]\n3. Distribute \\(4\\):\n\\[4 \\cdot 7 = 28\\]\n\\[4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x\\]\n\nNow, combine all these terms:\n\n\\[21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[21x^2 + 10x^2 - 6x^3 - 8x - 35x + 28 = -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\\]\n\nThus, the polynomial is:\n\n\\[d = 28, \\quad a = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43\\]\n\nWe are asked to find \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[8a = 8(-6) = -48\\]\n\\[4b = 4(31) = 124\\]\n\\[2c = 2(-43) = -86\\]\n\\[d = 28\\]\n\nTherefore, combining these results:\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = -48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 30\n\\]\n\nFinally, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]",
